Haakon Studebaker wrote:
> I think it'd be neat if NetHack allowed for multi-level mazes.

Yep. A couple years ago I made two (independent) suggestions like that.
One was a chapel with a library across three dungeon levels; rooms are
interconnected by random stairs or ladders across levels, thus building
a maze a'la "The Name of the Rose". The second were the Sewers, two or
three randomly generated levels below the castle that may have multiple
ladders per level leading to parallel sewer levels. Not all those ideas
match with the current implementation; there's some work required.

I seem to recall that, e.g., Adom supports some of those parallel mazes?

